OL,3,AHow video game remakes tap the power of
OL,4,Anostalgia
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe moment she saw footage from the
OL,7,Fremake of The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina
OL,8,Fof Time, Kacey Doran picked up her
OL,9,Fphone. She had to tell her sister.
OL,11,F"Have you seen this?" messaged Doran,
OL,12,Fexcitedly.
OL,14,FNearly 30 years ago, a 10-year-old
OL,15,FDoran had sat in front of her family's
OL,16,FTV, reading out the dialogue on screen
OL,17,Fto her sister, a year younger, as they
OL,18,Finched their way through the original
OL,19,FNintendo 64 game's sprawling,
OL,20,Fpuzzle-filled dungeons. Ocarina's
OL,21,Ffantasy-like story, and beautiful
OL,22,Fmusic, enthralled them both.
OL,23,APub: 30-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,107,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11904
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1793350458
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,AHow video game remakes tap the power of
OL,4,Anostalgia
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt was also the first game Doran ever
OL,7,Fcompleted. Now, countless memories
OL,8,Frushed back to her as she devoured
OL,9,Fclips of the fully redesigned version,
OL,10,Fdue to arrive on the Switch 2 later
OL,11,Fthis year.
OL,23,APub: 30-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG4/19
